{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## AC6 — `make verify` green, and all 6 boxes now ticked\n\n```\n20135 passed, 27 skipped, 48 warnings in 7597.64s (2:06:37)\nRC=0\n```\n\nRun at `693030cb9ab8b961cd1586a056f2d3ea1741989e`, worktree clean, in `.rebar/scratch/verify-19c3/`. Zero failures, zero errors.\n\nThat closes the last open criterion. ACs 1–5 were verified and filed earlier on this ticket; AC6 is the one that could only be answered by the full run, and it answers clean.\n\n**Pushed as Gerrit change [3194](https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/3194)**, tagged `rebar-session-6a3fecbb-7c5e-4e07-b1ba-7eb2bd09cb7c`. Awaiting `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1` before submit; this ticket closes only after the change merges.\n\n### One cross-check worth recording, because it nearly produced a false defect report\n\nThe AC1 sweep is word-anchored for a reason this run re-confirmed. A bare `git grep -F test_registry_heldout.py` reports a hit inside the **live** file `tests/unit/test_attest_registry.py` — which reads as a dangling reference to a module this story deleted. It is not. `attest` ends in `test`, so `test_attest_registry_heldout.py` contains `test_registry_heldout.py` as a substring starting at index 7. The anchored form `git grep -nE \"(^|[^A-Za-z0-9_])<basename>\"` returns 0 for that basename while still catching the genuine `code_arrow.json:16` literal.\n\nThis is the exact failure mode the AC1 amendment was written to prevent, encountered independently while verifying the amendment. The anchoring is load-bearing, not cosmetic.\n\nSeparately, the `.github/mechanism-baseline.json` stale row that AC1 permits as an exemption produced **no** hit, because the `--update-stale` drain required by AC5 removed it in this same commit. The exemption is now unused — correctly so, and harmless to leave in the AC text."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793513370949427332,"uuid":"08c70bbe-2f88-4301-97bb-9ac275bc8975"}